   $q$Based on the comparison, why do many families save the ferry for slow, sunny weekends?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The ferry only runs in the winter.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"Riders must wait for it, but they can enjoy the view.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The ferry is faster than the bridge on weekends.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The bridge is closed every weekend.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Riders must wait for it, but they can enjoy the view.$q$, $q$The passage says ferry riders can watch ducks and boats, but the ferry only leaves every thirty minutes, so riders may have to wait. That fits a slow day. The bridge is open "at any time of day or night," so it is not closed on weekends.$q$, 'draft', '743f1cbd-9fd6-54a3-a724-aa724342cd46')
